From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:33:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: qcom,snps-dwc3: describe a host VBUS supply

Describe an optional 5V port supply for fixed host controllers. The
external VBUS switch is a host resource, separate from the PHY digital
and analog power rails. Boards with a controllable port supply can keep
it off until the host is ready.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/qcom,snps-dwc3.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/qcom,snps-dwc3.yaml
@@ -74,6 +74,11 @@
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  vbus-supply:
+    description:
+      Optional 5V port supply for fixed host mode. This supply is controlled
+      by the USB host controller and is separate from the PHY power rails.
+
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
@@ -575,6 +580,16 @@
             - const: ss_phy_1
             - const: ss_phy_2
 
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        dr_mode:
+          const: host
+      required:
+        - dr_mode
+    else:
+      properties:
+        vbus-supply: false
+
 unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 examples:
